From 5c798e63e8342cfb2ecd7bd3c4e24994a6da5ad0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: facetimehd downstream <facetimehd-downstream@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 09/21] isp: harden the firmware command path

Merge fthd_isp_cmd() and fthd_isp_debug_cmd(), which differed only in
channel, timeout and status handling, and harden the shared path:

- validate request and response lengths, check that the completion
  points back at the request, and bound the response copy;
- make the completion wait uninterruptible: a submitted command cannot
  be cancelled, and a signal that ended the wait early let STREAMOFF
  release buffers the firmware still owned. Wake waiters with
  wake_up() accordingly, and only advance the ring index once an entry
  is actually submitted;
- when a command times out, keep its request memory allocated (the
  firmware may still complete into it), mark the firmware wedged and
  fail later commands with -EIO instead of waiting out every timeout.
  A stuck interrupt marks it wedged too, and a wedge errors the vb2
  queue so blocked readers wake up.
---
